frameguin (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add a Display group that switches the touchscreen off: at the mainboard's
    enable pad on the Laptop 13, whose panel has no off command of its own,
    and through the panel's command on the Laptop 12.
  * Add a battery window: temperature, cell voltages, alarms, cycle count and
    manufacturing date, asked of the pack itself where the EC's copy lags.
  * Add a parts window listing what was found — mainboard with its BIOS and
    EC versions, battery, touchpad, touchscreen — under the names Framework
    sells them by.
  * Rename the "Fingerprint reader" group "Power button LED", after the
    hardware the LED sits in rather than the EC's command for it.
  * Say why a window has no controls — no Framework hardware, a daemon that
    does not answer (with what systemd knows of the unit), or a board with
    nothing to control — instead of an empty window and a toast that is
    gone when the question is asked.
  * Leave the D-Bus error name out of a toast, keeping the daemon's sentence.
  * List the parts found in the troubleshooting report, in the words the
    daemon logs them.

 -- Valerii Myronov <valeriy@hey.com>  Sat, 29 Aug 2026 14:55:12 +0100

frameguin (0.1.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Name the charge rate in watts as well as amps.
  * Name a charge held at the limit as one, instead of reporting it as a
    discharge of tens of watts.
  * Hold the fingerprint LED dark when it is set to off, rather than flashing
    the previous brightness first.
  * Drop the keyboard backlight slider: the keyboard's own keys already set it.

 -- Valerii Myronov <valeriy@hey.com>  Tue, 25 Aug 2026 11:47:30 +0100

frameguin (0.1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add a charge speed control: charge at half or a quarter of the rate the
    battery is built for, at a rate set by hand, or with no cap at all.
  * Add an off level for the fingerprint LED.
  * Show the battery's charge and whether it is filling or draining, in the
    window and in the tray.

 -- Valerii Myronov <valeriy@hey.com>  Sat, 22 Aug 2026 17:57:59 +0100

frameguin (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Report which build is running: frameguin --version, an About window whose
    troubleshooting page carries a copyable hardware report, and a daemon
    GetBuild returning its version with the path it was started from.
  * install.sh installs a copy of itself, so a tarball installed through
    get.sh can be uninstalled without downloading it again, and warns when
    the other prefix already holds an install.

 -- Valerii Myronov <valeriy@hey.com>  Fri, 21 Aug 2026 10:18:09 +0100

